      "response": "Attack\n\n1. Behavior Summary  \nThe transaction repeatedly extracts 100 WETH from an unrelated address, converts it to ETH, and routes proceeds to the MEV bot. This is unauthorized fund draining, not a normal swap.\n\n2. Call Sequence Analysis  \nZero-input SushiSwap routes invoke the bot’s swap callback. Each callback executes `transferFrom` for 100 WETH from `0x31d...13e1` to the bot, followed by WETH withdrawal. Repetition compounds the theft. Additional ETH is sent to beaverbuild and another bot.\n\n3. Malicious Indicators  \nZero amounts, null recipients, fabricated callback deltas, repeated victim transfers, and missing meaningful swap output strongly indicate exploitation. Historical similarity: Low, because no matching example was provided.",
